{"term":"abstract","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b941a4c7c59acdd215","definition":"An abridgement or summary of a longer publication.","example":"An analysis and abstract of every treatise he had read.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abstract of title"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstract#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ba3ea458260a045dc3","definition":"Something that concentrates in itself the qualities of a larger item, or multiple items.","example":"Man, the abstract Of all perfection, which the workmanship Of Heaven hath modeled.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abstract of title"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstract#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4ed11fe9ddfa827c14","definition":"An abstraction; an abstract term; that which is abstract.","example":"Thus the concrete like has its abstract likeness; the concretes, father and son, have the abstracts, paternity and filiation.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abstract of title"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstract#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0fb2f8cff1644f320f","definition":"The theoretical way of looking at things; something that exists only in idealized form.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abstract of title"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstract#English","